      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this allows the host VM to crash pKVM in its current form:\n1) comment says \"@vaddr is aligned down to the PAGE_SIZE, and the lookup size is PAGE_SIZE.\"\n2) pkvm_pgtable_lookup is called by pkvm_host_mmu_handle_fault() which gets gpa from `gpa \u003d vmcs_read64(GUEST_PHYSICAL_ADDRESS);` and this gpa dosn\u0027t have to be page aligned\n3) in normal case it would not be a problem although due to `.end   \u003d ALIGN(vaddr + size, PAGE_SIZE)` the walker will walk two pages instead of one and since lookup_walker() returns PGTABLE_WALK_DONE on the first leaf no issue will be triggered.\n4) but if host faults on big address `data.end \u003e pkvm_pgtable_max_size(pgt))` check could fail and crash pKVM, so it is probably better to `BUG_ON(pkvm_pgtable_walk(pgt, ALIGN_DOWN(vaddr, PAGE_SIZE)...`\n\nand also probably in `pkvm_host_mmu_handle_fault()` reject `gpa \u003e\u003d pkvm_pgtable_max_size` or it is somehow already prevented?",
